# Nature Sounds Therapy

> A father-and-son duo recording authentic outdoor nature sounds across Central
> Europe — forests, rivers, birdsong, wind, crickets. Real field recordings for
> sleep, relaxation and focus. No music, no narration, no AI-generated audio.

## Who we are

Nature Sounds Therapy (NST) is run by a father and his son, who is on the
autism spectrum. The forests, mountain trails and the sound of running water
are where he finds his greatest peace — these recording trips became their
shared world. Every recording comes from a specific real place, captured on a
specific day, often in one continuous take of many hours.

## What makes the recordings different

- 100% real field recordings: no music, no narration, no loops, no AI
- Long continuous takes (often 7–12 hours from a single location overnight)
- Locations: Poland (Bieszczady, Karkonosze, Izery, Masurian Lakes, Baltic
  coast), German borderlands, Slovak Tatras
- Gear: Zoom F3 (32-bit float), Sennheiser MKE 600, Rode NT1, Panasonic
  Lumix S5, Insta360 Pro (360° VR)
- Formats: 4K scenic films, black-screen sleep versions, 360° VR, podcasts

